// DAVOF static gate 1 on a POLYHEDRAL mesh (mesh: poly -> cfMesh pMesh,
// 2026-10-12). This file REPLACES sphereNormal3D.parameter for mesh: poly
// studies (workflow/Snakefile PARAM_FILE), so it carries the hex values plus
// the surface of the cfMesh box (SURFACE_FILE, system/meshDict.template).
//
// The same sphere (R = 1 mm, centre off every mesh symmetry plane) in the same
// 4 mm box as the hexahedral ladder; N_CELLS is the SAME ladder: cfMesh is asked
// for maxCellSize = h/2^(-1/3), h = DOMAIN_LENGTH/N_CELLS (the derived token
// CFMESH_CELL_SIZE), because its dual cells at the interface measure 2^(-1/3)
// maxCellSize (the pin of workflow/README.md): the interface resolution is the
// hex ladder's h = 200/100/50/25 um; the mean over all cells (DELTA_X) is smaller. Two alpha sources:
// quadraticFaces (q = 2) and detrixheAslam (q = 1); exactSphere is hex-only
// (davofState.C FatalErrors on a cell that is not an axis-aligned box) and the
// plane indicator is not part of the mesh-class comparison. The cross-check
// runs OpenFOAM's geometricVoF plicRDF, gradAlpha and isoAlpha on the identical
// alpha field of each source. Serial; cfMesh needs jemalloc preloaded on the
// laptop (LEIA_PMESH_PRELOAD, workflow/README.md), not on Lichtenberg.
values
{
    solver (leiaTestDavofNormal);

    N_CELLS ( 20 40 80 160 );

    DOMAIN_LENGTH ( 0.004 );

    SURFACE_FILE ( box4mm-faces.stl );

    DAVOF_ALPHA_SOURCE ( quadraticFaces detrixheAslam );

    DAVOF_CROSS_CHECK ( geometricVoF );

    DAVOF_CURV_MODEL_1 ( none );

    DAVOF_CURV_MODEL_2 ( none );

    DAVOF_REGEN_ARM ( none );

    DAVOF_REGEN_ITER ( 1 );

    DAVOF_REGEN_FEEDBACK ( own );

    DAVOF_REGEN_REFIT ( true );

    DAVOF_REGEN_ORIGIN ( volume );
}
